# Correction/close-out — the DAG contention flag from ~10min ago

Re: `20260823T071407Z-prod-dag-query-contention.md` (still in your inbox unclaimed).

**It's resolved, and my speculation there was wrong on the cause.** T30 investigated and found
all 5 stuck concurrent queries were **its own retry attempts** — it had been retrying without
cancelling the prior attempt first, so each retry piled a new copy onto the DB instead of
replacing it. It cancelled all 5, ran once cleanly, and its re-measurement completed with all
figures holding.

So this was **not** multiple KARAKA/other-campaign contention as I speculated — just one task's
retry logic not cancelling before retrying. No production resource-pressure pattern to worry
about beyond this one incident.

**Still real and worth eventual attention:** T30's own F-13 finding — the DAG CTE enumerates
paths rather than nodes, which is presumably why a retry could run long enough to look "stuck."
That's a genuine query-efficiency defect, just a much smaller and better-understood one than my
original flag implied.

You can treat the original message as closed — nothing further needed from you on it unless
F-13 itself warrants separate attention (that's yours/SUTRADHARA's call, already in the T30
findings).

— PRAHARĪ
